# supabase/setup/00_full_setup.sql is compared against the generator's output
# byte for byte by `npm run setup:check`, and scripts/generate-setup-bundle.mjs
# joins its own header and separator lines with "\n" while copying the
# migration bodies through verbatim. Handed a CRLF working copy — which is what
# core.autocrlf=true does on Windows — that comparison fails on every fresh
# clone even when nothing has drifted, and a check that cries wolf is a check
# people stop reading. It is the only thing standing between us and a stale
# bundle; it had silently fallen eleven migrations behind once already.
#
# Pinning the SQL to LF in the working tree, not just in the repository, is
# what keeps the two byte-identical.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, different victim: a shell script checked out with CRLF has a
# carriage return on the end of its shebang, and the kernel looks for an
# interpreter called "bash\r". The error names a path that is plainly correct,
# which is the worst kind. supabase/tests/event_tickets_functions.sh is the
# only one here, and it is run by hand on the machine that cloned the repo.
*.sh text eol=lf
